1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,280
Short version, if you just got here.

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:07,120
I was three weeks behind on my rental car
when a passenger left two hundred grand in

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:09,400
my trunk, and I took it to the police.

4
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:14,120
The passenger's daughter, Laura, showed
up swearing her dad didn't steal it.

5
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:18,800
Then her dad's boss got on speakerphone
and offered me twenty grand to sign a

6
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:22,240
statement and go home. But his
theft report had a problem.

7
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:23,840
I didn't sign.

8
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:28,240
"Before anybody signs anything," I
said, "can I show you something?"

9
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:30,160
I held my phone up to Detective Bell.

10
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:31,800
The ride receipt.

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,920
Pickup at ten-forty.

12
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:36,800
"Your report was filed
at nine-ten," I said.

13
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:39,440
"But at nine-ten, he still had the bag.

14
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:42,200
He put it in my trunk an
hour and a half later.

15
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:45,520
So how did Mister Brandt
already know it was missing?"

16
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:47,520
The speakerphone went very quiet.

17
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,160
You could hear somebody
breathing on the other end.

18
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:53,960
Then Vince reached over,
switched it off, and said,

19
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:56,560
"Mister Brandt's attorney
will be in touch."

20
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:58,480
Detective Bell didn't even look at him.

21
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:00,320
She was looking at me,

22
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:03,760
the way you look at somebody who
just made your night a lot longer.

23
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:08,280
She pulled one stack of bills out of the
bag and turned it over under the desk

24
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:11,840
lamp. The paper band was
stamped with two letters.

25
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:13,560
B M.

26
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:15,800
"Brandt Markets," she said.

27
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:20,080
"Funny. Banks don't wrap their cash
with a grocery store's initials.

28
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:21,800
Somebody wraps their own.

29
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:24,160
Cash that never went through a bank."

30
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:27,960
Laura made this sound,
half laugh, half sob.

31
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:31,440
Vince picked up his phone and
walked out without another word.

32
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:34,680
Turns out, that's exactly
what Harold had found.

33
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:38,200
Years of cash that never showed
up in the company's books.

34
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:41,040
He was on his way to tell
federal investigators.

35
00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:43,600
And his boss had filed
a theft report first,

36
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:47,640
so that when Harold finally talked,
nobody would ever believe him.

37
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:50,840
Harold was released the next afternoon.

38
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:54,040
Laura had told me that if the bag
got to the police that night,

39
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:56,053
her dad would go to prison.

40
00:01:56,107 --> 00:01:57,320
It got there.

41
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:59,160
And that's what got him out.

42
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:03,080
Brandt's lawyers got busy, and
the investigators got busier.

43
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:04,160
The money?

44
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:05,280
Evidence.

45
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:09,240
Locked in a room somewhere,
with no reward for anybody.

46
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:12,880
On Monday morning, the rental
company came and took the car.

47
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:15,480
A guy with a clipboard
walked around it twice,

48
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:18,880
checked the mileage, and drove
off without saying much.

49
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:22,200
I stood in the parking lot and
watched it turn the corner.

50
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:23,240
No car.

51
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:24,280
No job.

52
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:26,840
The hospital bill still on my fridge.

53
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:28,960
Later, Laura texted me.

54
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:31,400
Just a photo of her dad
at his kitchen table,

55
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:35,080
eating a plate of spaghetti,
and the words "thank you."

56
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:37,600
I must have looked at it for ten minutes.

57
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:42,560
That night, for the first time in
months, I didn't lie awake doing math.

58
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:44,040
I lost the car.

59
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,840
But I slept fine.

60
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:48,680
That's ending three of four.

61
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:51,880
Okay, so now you know
where the money came from.

62
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:55,347
But there was something in that
bag worth way more than cash,

63
00:02:55,373 --> 00:02:57,360
and I haven't told you about it yet.

64
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:59,360
Go back and pick another path.

65
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:01,800
The full map is pinned in the comments.
